1
00:00,290 --> 00:05,629
Oppo has just launched a foldable phone that's so thin, it only just fits a USB-C port.

2
00:05,809 --> 00:09,210
I'm not exaggerating. The inside of a USB-C port is 2.4mm.

3
00:09,529 --> 00:12,169
Once you add in the structural housing, you get to about 4mm.

4
00:12,449 --> 00:16,570
The Oppo Find N5 is 4.2mm thick when unfolded.

5
00:16,629 --> 00:19,010
And somehow, that's not even the best bit.

6
00:19,089 --> 00:22,710
It's also meant to be much faster than the competition, with a longer battery, better cameras,

7
00:22,850 --> 00:27,510
along with just a whole load of tech that no one expected, like new signal enhancement.

8
00:27,510 --> 00:30,809
The most powerful image generation that I've ever seen on a phone,

9
00:30,949 --> 00:33,609
and even the ability to integrate into the Apple ecosystem.

10
00:33,929 --> 00:37,969
So, let's pin it head-to-head against Samsung, who makes the best-selling foldables,

11
00:38,189 --> 00:41,530
to find out if Oppo is actually about to massacre the market.

12
00:41,829 --> 00:45,689
And right from the off, Oppo lands its very first blow when it comes to the unboxing.

13
00:45,929 --> 00:47,009
Because this is what you get.

14
00:47,149 --> 00:54,229
An 80-watt charging brick, a USB A to C cable, and a case, which does feel premium, but also very light.

15
00:54,229 --> 01:00,009
I guess that makes sense, since designing a phone like this and then slapping a chunkmeister case onto it would be very ironic.

16
01:01,070 --> 01:06,250
Now, compare that to Samsung's package, which literally just comes with the phone and a USB-C cable.

17
01:06,409 --> 01:10,349
You're getting about $80 of extra free value in the box with Oppo.

18
01:10,450 --> 01:12,590
Plus, pre-installed screen protector on the front,

19
01:12,769 --> 01:15,670
which is one of those things that probably cost them about 50 cents to do.

20
01:15,790 --> 01:20,209
But to you, the user, it's one fairly major less thing that you need to worry about.

21
01:20,209 --> 01:24,109
And you know what? Oppo continues the onslaught when it comes to the build.

22
01:24,530 --> 01:26,170
And it ain't close.

23
01:26,409 --> 01:29,510
Both phones have a pretty tough custom aluminium alloy frame.

24
01:29,670 --> 01:33,950
They've both got fantastic feeling hinges that allow you to stop at almost any point in the motion.

25
01:34,109 --> 01:37,290
But then it kind of feels like Oppo runs away with it.

26
01:37,409 --> 01:42,430
Their front display is imbued with ceramic, which we've seen on quite a few phones does increase structural strength.

27
01:42,590 --> 01:43,709
It's got better water resistance.

28
01:43,909 --> 01:48,569
While Samsung's phone can take immersion, this thing can go further and actually take high-pressure jets.

29
01:48,569 --> 01:54,129
And extreme temperatures to beat for my extreme lifestyle.

30
01:55,629 --> 02:00,629
And just zooming out for a second, the fact that it's even close, let alone a head in terms of durability,

31
02:00,629 --> 02:08,129
is quite insane considering that Oppo is also almost 30% thinner, in part thanks to some careful re-engineering of the motherboard.

32
02:08,349 --> 02:12,830
It's 10 grams lighter, all while having a significantly less visible crease than Samsung.

33
02:12,969 --> 02:19,909
Oppo's saying that the crease on this phone is 10% narrower and 50% shallower than the crease on their last phone, which was already gray.

34
02:19,909 --> 02:27,669
It doesn't look that different to me, but it's clearly vastly superior to the Samsung, which you will notice every time you open the thing.

35
02:27,830 --> 02:34,490
So yeah, when you use this phone for the first time, it is absolutely one of those moments that just makes you peer back over at the Samsung

36
02:34,490 --> 02:38,590
and truly reconsider how much this company is actually trying.

37
02:38,889 --> 02:45,229
The only two downsides on the Oppo are that, one, they've had to replace the glass on the back for a thinner fiber material,

38
02:45,229 --> 02:50,409
which they've masked pretty well with this whole marbly texture, but does still feel a little plasticky.

39
02:50,669 --> 02:55,930
And then two, that for some reason, while Oppo decided to completely full send this thing in terms of water resistance,

40
02:56,229 --> 02:59,550
they've actually got no certification in terms of dust resistance.

41
02:59,830 --> 03:03,189
Well, at the very least, Samsung does have a basic IP4 rating.

42
03:04,009 --> 03:09,610
But then you take the phones out into the real world and you start to notice something kind of unusual when it comes to battery.

43
03:09,909 --> 03:13,770
So the Oppo uses a brand new type of battery that we've only really started seeing recently,

44
03:13,770 --> 03:17,650
a silicon carbon battery with the highest silicon content so far.

45
03:17,750 --> 03:22,169
You can think of silicon carbon batteries as just more energy dense than traditional lithium-ion batteries.

46
03:22,370 --> 03:28,389
And so what this means is that within less space, this phone has managed to squeeze in a 5,600 milliamp hour capacity

47
03:28,389 --> 03:30,490
compared to Samsung's 4,400.

48
03:30,770 --> 03:32,110
That's a massive difference.

49
03:32,389 --> 03:35,289
Now, I did find that if you push both phones to their limit,

50
03:35,430 --> 03:38,469
then the Oppo will still actually drain just as fast as the Samsung.

51
03:38,710 --> 03:42,270
And that kind of makes sense, given that the chip on this phone can draw more power

52
03:42,270 --> 03:45,110
and silicon carbon batteries are better at providing that power.

53
03:45,370 --> 03:49,990
But if you assume average use, a bit of gaming, a bit of social media, a bit of browsing and music,

54
03:50,150 --> 03:52,629
Oppo will outlast Sammy 10 times out of 10.

55
03:52,930 --> 03:57,030
Not to mention the other flip side of this more conductive battery is faster charging.

56
03:57,210 --> 04:01,069
While Samsung takes around 90 minutes to fully charge, Oppo takes about 50.

57
04:01,210 --> 04:05,409
And remember, in that time, it's charging up a 25% bigger cell.

58
04:05,409 --> 04:07,590
Plus faster wireless charging too.

59
04:07,810 --> 04:12,370
50 watts versus 15 watts, which frankly is just embarrassing for Samsung

60
04:12,370 --> 04:16,410
since Oppo is doing all that with a new coil specifically made for the phone

61
04:16,410 --> 04:18,670
because it's 40% thinner than normal.

62
04:19,189 --> 04:22,110
Okay, so that's four points to Oppo, zero to Samsung.

63
04:22,689 --> 04:24,810
But fine, Samsung's got screens at least, right?

64
04:25,009 --> 04:26,769
I mean, that's kind of what they do.

65
04:27,029 --> 04:29,689
Literally every TV in this house is a Samsung TV.

66
04:29,689 --> 04:29,829
Nope.

67
04:32,829 --> 04:37,170
And it's really funny because Oppo has kind of just pulled a Samsung here.

68
04:37,410 --> 04:41,250
So when you open both phones up, you'll immediately notice that Oppo's is the bigger screen.

69
04:41,410 --> 04:44,329
It's higher resolution and it's largely speaking creaseless.

70
04:44,490 --> 04:47,529
But as well as that, you know that anti-reflective screen coating

71
04:47,529 --> 04:50,850
that Samsung's kind of become famous for on their S series flagships?

72
04:50,930 --> 04:54,189
Well, Oppo has employed something very similar on their inner display here.

73
04:54,550 --> 04:56,490
And Samsung hasn't.

74
04:56,490 --> 05:00,470
This isn't quite as effective as the anti-reflective coating Samsung uses on their bar phones,

75
05:00,670 --> 05:03,850
but it's better than the no-coating that they have on their foldables.

76
05:04,069 --> 05:07,050
Actually making Oppo now the one with the more readable screen.

77
05:07,290 --> 05:10,370
Oh yeah, and the Oppo also has the better cover screen on the front.

78
05:10,670 --> 05:14,829
See, if you look at Samsung in isolation, it feels like they're making really good progress here.

79
05:14,990 --> 05:16,490
Their first foldable looked like this.

80
05:16,670 --> 05:19,509
And each generation, we've seen this cover screen get a little bigger,

81
05:19,670 --> 05:22,790
a little closer to the edges, and the hinge on the side being pulled in

82
05:22,790 --> 05:26,189
to more and more closely resemble just a normal bar phone.

83
05:26,189 --> 05:29,149
But it's only when you put it side by side with the Oppo that you're reminded,

84
05:29,810 --> 05:32,230
oh yeah, this, this is a bar phone.

85
05:32,649 --> 05:36,470
Oppo is wide enough to feel like a genuinely natural aspect ratio for typing.

86
05:36,670 --> 05:40,089
It weighs almost the exact same as a standard iPhone 16 Pro Max.

87
05:40,230 --> 05:42,250
And it's got normal phone thickness too.

88
05:42,370 --> 05:45,629
So I don't feel like I'm carrying around a third leg in my pocket.

89
05:45,889 --> 05:47,889
And so seeing that you can have all of that,

90
05:48,269 --> 05:50,350
that suddenly reminds you Samsung isn't quite there.

91
05:50,509 --> 05:53,069
I don't really like these two weird looking corners.

92
05:53,069 --> 05:55,889
And also Samsung's displays are a bit brighter when you're outdoors.

93
05:56,290 --> 05:57,769
But, you know, if I had to pick one,

94
05:57,990 --> 06:01,069
I would still on balance prefer the Oppo's set of screens.

95
06:01,629 --> 06:04,709
So it's turning into a bit of a bloodbath right now.

96
06:05,209 --> 06:06,189
What about performance?

97
06:07,949 --> 06:09,029
Yeah, the Oppo has that too.

98
06:09,410 --> 06:12,110
The thing's using the next generation Snapdragon 8 Elite chip,

99
06:12,209 --> 06:14,470
as opposed to the Samsung, which uses last year's chip.

100
06:14,589 --> 06:18,610
This is basically powered by the thing that you could expect Samsung's next foldable

101
06:18,610 --> 06:20,290
that will come out in the summer to be powered by.

102
06:20,290 --> 06:26,209
And so it's not hugely surprising to see that it came out a good 35% faster when we ran a stress test.

103
06:26,370 --> 06:28,550
But the thing that I thought was even more interesting here is that

104
06:28,550 --> 06:32,310
even though Oppo is the one that's rocking the higher power consumption chip,

105
06:32,550 --> 06:35,870
that performance gap only widened with prolonged use.

106
06:36,050 --> 06:39,949
Because by the end of this stress test, it was actually 50% faster than Samsung,

107
06:40,230 --> 06:41,750
which is frankly bonkers.

108
06:41,949 --> 06:45,069
It felt like such a huge jump that I had to rerun the stress test again

109
06:45,069 --> 06:49,829
to find not quite as large a gap, but still 40% by the end of the test.

110
06:50,009 --> 06:54,009
Now, there's a pretty decent chance that you'll never even notice that 30 to 40% gap

111
06:54,009 --> 06:56,310
because just scrolling around the homepages,

112
06:56,709 --> 06:58,790
Samsung is often the one that can feel a bit snappier,

113
06:58,889 --> 07:00,910
just down to the way that they've tuned their animations.

114
07:01,189 --> 07:04,209
But to me, it does feel like in all the areas where speed is important,

115
07:04,509 --> 07:06,569
like how fast apps open when you click them

116
07:06,569 --> 07:08,889
and how fast your camera shutter can capture shots

117
07:08,889 --> 07:12,350
and how fast your image processing applies after you've taken those shots,

118
07:12,490 --> 07:13,949
Oppo is generally ahead.

119
07:13,949 --> 07:15,470
So what about the software?

120
07:16,750 --> 07:19,910
I have to say, the way that Oppo handles multitasking,

121
07:20,129 --> 07:22,009
it remains the gold standard.

122
07:22,250 --> 07:23,889
So let's say, for example, that you're on Netflix

123
07:23,889 --> 07:27,230
and then you also want a browser tab to do a little shopping on the side.

124
07:27,810 --> 07:28,029
Bam!

125
07:28,189 --> 07:31,750
You can do both in their optimal aspect ratios, fully open at once.

126
07:31,889 --> 07:34,509
But now you've decided what you fancy watching is Dragon Ball Z.

127
07:34,709 --> 07:35,470
Search on Netflix.

128
07:35,750 --> 07:36,870
Oh, it's not there.

129
07:37,069 --> 07:39,350
So let's pull up our sponsor, Surfshark VPN.

130
07:39,689 --> 07:41,310
You just drag that icon into the mix

131
07:41,310 --> 07:44,649
and all of a sudden, three different apps all open at the same time.

132
07:44,750 --> 07:48,370
And all I need to do now is to go into Surfshark to change my location to Japan.

133
07:48,629 --> 07:50,069
It's genuinely as simple as that.

134
07:50,149 --> 07:55,910
And now if we pop back to Netflix, it will reload and Dragon Ball Z, there it is.

135
07:56,029 --> 07:57,449
We can click it, we can watch it.

136
07:57,449 --> 08:00,410
It completely opens up the content that you can get into.

137
08:00,689 --> 08:01,589
And it ramps up.

138
08:01,670 --> 08:04,649
Because then, let's say that you've decided what it is that you want to buy over here.

139
08:04,769 --> 08:07,910
Now you're left with the incredibly fiddly task of adding your details in.

140
08:08,009 --> 08:10,490
Except it's not fiddly at all here.

141
08:10,670 --> 08:14,490
Thanks in part to this phone's insane multitasking and in part Surfshark,

142
08:14,610 --> 08:17,370
which also comes with an alternate ID feature.

143
08:17,509 --> 08:20,629
Anytime that you want to sign up to a site that you're not completely sure about,

144
08:20,769 --> 08:25,050
it generates an entirely new online identity for you that's immediately copyable.

145
08:25,050 --> 08:28,930
Which means you can still get your communications forwarded to your real email, for example,

146
08:29,189 --> 08:32,289
just without revealing those details to companies that you don't trust.

147
08:32,429 --> 08:37,070
Go to surfshark.com slash boss and use the code boss to get Surfshark for less than $3 a month

148
08:37,070 --> 08:40,009
with an extra four months for free and a 30-day money-back guarantee.

149
08:40,350 --> 08:41,970
So the multitasking is sick.

150
08:42,169 --> 08:45,169
And there's a few more things that Oppo software does that just feel clever.

151
08:45,429 --> 08:46,370
Like file doc.

152
08:46,529 --> 08:50,330
Basically just a dump to drop anything of interest that you're trying to collect together

153
08:50,330 --> 08:52,750
to put into an email or share into a WhatsApp group.

154
08:52,750 --> 08:57,309
It's basically just a clipboard, but done in a very intuitive way that actually saves you time.

155
08:57,409 --> 08:59,649
And then you've got this whole Oppo O Plus Connect thing,

156
08:59,850 --> 09:03,649
which to their credit probably is the easiest way that I've used on Android

157
09:03,649 --> 09:09,370
to send full quality files complete with all metadata to an iPhone with no Wi-Fi connection.

158
09:09,570 --> 09:14,210
But equally, let's be very honest, this is still a long shot from native Apple integration,

159
09:14,549 --> 09:18,629
while also feeling very much like a knockoff version of Apple's solution.

160
09:18,629 --> 09:22,730
And I think just generally, that is one of the things that I don't like about this software.

161
09:23,049 --> 09:24,610
It feels a little cheap.

162
09:24,730 --> 09:28,070
Like you go into an app folder, you get recommended apps at the bottom.

163
09:28,289 --> 09:31,909
If this was a $200 phone, fair enough, but not at these kinds of prices.

164
09:32,230 --> 09:35,669
Sometimes those recommended apps just fail to load, which looks even worse.

165
09:35,870 --> 09:38,169
Oppo's app market pings you to get your attention.

166
09:38,350 --> 09:40,190
And even when you eventually give in and accept,

167
09:40,470 --> 09:43,429
it's not a very intuitive app to be navigating at all,

168
09:43,529 --> 09:46,529
which does make me feel like Samsung's software is more sophisticated.

169
09:46,529 --> 09:50,169
And while this phone doesn't yet have the One UI 7 update,

170
09:50,350 --> 09:53,669
knowing that it will get it, and just how much I love that software,

171
09:53,809 --> 09:56,789
does make me veer towards Uncle Sam in this category.

172
09:56,889 --> 10:02,149
All finished off by the fact that Samsung has a definitively better ecosystem of surrounding products,

173
10:02,210 --> 10:03,210
if you're outside of China,

174
10:03,429 --> 10:06,429
and seven years of major Android version upgrades,

175
10:06,850 --> 10:08,470
Oppo phones tend to get four.

176
10:08,769 --> 10:11,269
It's pretty much the same story when it comes to AI features.

177
10:11,509 --> 10:14,549
Like this Oppo phone is doing some very interesting stuff.

178
10:14,549 --> 10:18,070
Like, you can pull up any photo on this phone, click Enhance Clarity,

179
10:18,629 --> 10:20,690
boom, straight up detail upgrade.

180
10:20,830 --> 10:23,590
And the thing's got this whole separate app called AI Studio,

181
10:23,909 --> 10:26,549
which is very cool and very strange.

182
10:26,669 --> 10:28,830
So you get a bunch of free credits when you buy the phone,

183
10:28,970 --> 10:31,169
and then you can spend those credits doing things like

184
10:31,169 --> 10:33,370
inserting yourself next to celebrities.

185
10:33,710 --> 10:35,509
It works, kind of.

186
10:35,769 --> 10:38,169
Although I am curious, are people using stuff like this

187
10:38,169 --> 10:40,309
to make it seem like they actually met those people?

188
10:40,309 --> 10:43,490
And if they're not, then what are they doing with it?

189
10:43,590 --> 10:47,110
I've managed to turn myself into a rather handsome, if I might say, pirate.

190
10:47,389 --> 10:51,190
This is powerful AI, hence the credits to stop people spamming it.

191
10:51,269 --> 10:52,870
And it's not just creating brand new images,

192
10:53,110 --> 10:56,490
you can also reimagine existing images into new styles.

193
10:56,769 --> 10:59,009
And it is very, very effective.

194
10:59,529 --> 11:02,190
Highest quality image generation I've seen baked into a phone.

195
11:02,309 --> 11:05,269
Interesting, though, that it's given Drisha an entirely new ethnicity.

196
11:05,730 --> 11:09,070
There's a good chance that this is just down to how the AI has been trained.

197
11:09,070 --> 11:11,169
And aside from that, just generally across the phone,

198
11:11,549 --> 11:15,710
let's not forget that Oppo has a lot of equivalence to Samsung's AI features.

199
11:15,889 --> 11:17,029
Like, let's say you're in a document.

200
11:17,269 --> 11:19,769
Just like Samsung, there's a whole load of writing tools.

201
11:19,990 --> 11:21,889
Oppo's got AI replies for messages.

202
11:22,149 --> 11:25,009
They've even got an AI that can write Instagram captions for you.

203
11:25,210 --> 11:28,269
At the same time, I really hope it doesn't come to me having to use that.

204
11:28,409 --> 11:33,129
It's just that, on average, Oppo's implementation feels about a year behind.

205
11:33,450 --> 11:37,190
A lot of the AI features are either coming soon, or they're quite situational.

206
11:37,190 --> 11:40,450
They work sometimes, and then, for some reason, not at other times.

207
11:40,610 --> 11:41,789
I mean, let's not kid ourselves.

208
11:41,950 --> 11:44,110
I wouldn't exactly call Samsung's AI reliable.

209
11:44,370 --> 11:48,370
But at the same time, if I had to lean on one of these, I would still rather lean on this.

210
11:48,470 --> 11:52,669
And similarly, one of the things Oppo is boasting loudest about with this phone is link boost.

211
11:52,830 --> 11:56,850
This AI system combined with a 360-degree antenna architecture,

212
11:57,029 --> 12:00,570
which should improve signal by 20% to 30% in weak areas.

213
12:00,570 --> 12:03,909
But I've tested it multiple times in multiple locations,

214
12:03,909 --> 12:07,610
and I can't see any consistent, tangible benefit over the Samsung,

215
12:07,789 --> 12:10,809
which makes me feel like you probably won't notice the difference either.

216
12:11,009 --> 12:12,850
Okay, just before we finish this off with the cameras,

217
12:13,230 --> 12:16,090
I do just want to mention speakers, because they're important to me.

218
12:16,210 --> 12:20,629
One thing that you will just generally notice as tech gets thinner is speakers get worse,

219
12:20,750 --> 12:24,549
because they have less space to be able to push air to create the sound.

220
12:24,549 --> 12:26,230
And that's the case here.

221
12:26,450 --> 12:28,809
Oppo's done a good job, I'd say, to make it not suck,

222
12:29,029 --> 12:32,769
but it definitely lacks the satisfying richness of Samsung speakers.

223
12:33,490 --> 12:38,570
Now, cameras are one area that I was expecting Oppo to absolutely destroy Samsung at.

224
12:38,789 --> 12:42,990
But when you use this thing, you realize that cameras are one thing that Oppo has

225
12:42,990 --> 12:46,730
majorly compromised on, on this phone specifically, to hit their thinness goals.

226
12:46,850 --> 12:50,590
The main camera is decent, but I do think Samsung has more true-to-life colors,

227
12:50,789 --> 12:52,549
and also, it's just a bit more flattering.

228
12:52,549 --> 12:56,889
Oppo has this quite crunchy, contrasty look that I don't think is forever on.

229
12:56,970 --> 12:59,470
The ultrawide camera on Oppo is just bad.

230
12:59,629 --> 13:01,970
It's an 8-megapixel camera compared to Samsung's 12,

231
13:02,210 --> 13:04,610
and that is a massive resolution gap.

232
13:04,730 --> 13:07,370
Oppo's just doesn't even look fit for a 2025 phone.

233
13:07,509 --> 13:11,029
That said, Oppo does have a better internal selfie camera than Samsung,

234
13:11,250 --> 13:12,669
which is, I mean, it's not hard.

235
13:12,730 --> 13:15,090
I'm pretty sure my fridge has a better camera than this thing.

236
13:15,169 --> 13:18,549
Since Samsung decided to go for an under-display camera that's capped at 4,

237
13:18,669 --> 13:20,730
I repeat, 4 megapixels.

238
13:20,730 --> 13:22,750
And Oppo also has better zoom.

239
13:22,909 --> 13:27,529
Both have 3x optical zoom, but Oppo's 3x optical zoom camera is 50 megapixel,

240
13:27,649 --> 13:28,769
compared to Samsung's 10.

241
13:28,990 --> 13:30,409
And boy, you can tell.

242
13:30,509 --> 13:33,250
There is some more fake AI enhancement going on on Oppo,

243
13:33,409 --> 13:36,149
but even just that aside, you can tell there's more information too.

244
13:36,370 --> 13:41,389
Also, shout out to Oppo for turning this telephoto zoom camera into the macro camera too,

245
13:41,649 --> 13:43,830
because most phones just use their ultrawide camera.

246
13:43,970 --> 13:47,509
But Oppo has given this telephoto camera a super short focusing distance,

247
13:47,509 --> 13:50,009
so it fills that role instead of the ultrawide.

248
13:50,129 --> 13:51,269
And this is the way to go.

249
13:51,429 --> 13:54,470
You get less distortion on your subject when you're shooting from further away.

250
13:54,629 --> 13:58,610
And it also means that you can just get closer without physically needing to get closer,

251
13:58,769 --> 14:02,269
which is less fiddly, and you're blocking less of the light on that subject.

252
14:02,669 --> 14:05,269
This Samsung doesn't even have a proper macro mode.

253
14:05,350 --> 14:09,269
That said, nothing beats Samsung's portrait mode and its ability to detect depth.

254
14:09,269 --> 14:13,889
Can you see how Oppo has decided to blur this entire phone booth as if it's really far away from me?

255
14:14,190 --> 14:15,850
Except for those two stickers.

256
14:16,970 --> 14:18,049
Interesting choice, Oppo.

257
14:18,330 --> 14:20,190
So, cameras are about a draw.

258
14:20,389 --> 14:22,950
The camera app on the Oppo is smoother, which is a nice plus,

259
14:23,070 --> 14:25,429
but it's not a consistently better camera than Sammy.

260
14:25,629 --> 14:27,309
And so that leaves us with a score.

261
14:27,549 --> 14:29,490
6.5 points to 3.5.

262
14:29,710 --> 14:31,210
And the numbers aren't everything.

263
14:31,549 --> 14:34,470
But would I pick the Oppo if I had a choice over the Samsung?

264
14:35,529 --> 14:36,509
Yes, I would.

265
14:36,509 --> 14:40,809
The way they've managed to fit something so much faster, longer-lasting, faster-charging

266
14:40,809 --> 14:44,330
into a body that's at least a couple of generations slimmer is no joke.

267
14:44,429 --> 14:45,289
But it's not a whitewash.

268
14:45,590 --> 14:49,649
Software matters, and software is where Samsung does revive some of its dignity.
